{
  "content": {
    "arguments": "$ARGUMENTS",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "id": "7d0560ce-f45a-4606-9581-c18c2e4067bf",
        "text": "Use the Bash tool. The Pebbles CLI at \"{PEBBLES_CLI}\" is the ONLY sanctioned way to change spec files — never edit .pebble files directly."
      },
      {
        "id": "3bf5ef0a-ddc2-4054-adf0-90599241917a",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Spec mutation contract (rules/system/spec-mutation-contract)"
      },
      {
        "id": "570144ee-4a11-4020-ac65-e0f45d8b33c1",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Status discipline (rules/system/status-discipline)"
      },
      {
        "id": "7ed6670d-0598-4517-aa4d-7b3e4f16a16e",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Findings are the append-only evidence log (rules/system/findings-as-evidence)"
      },
      {
        "id": "adf3d8a5-5594-43ec-ba28-606cf0b8118b",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Implementation standard (rules/system/implementation-standard)"
      },
      {
        "id": "f7f0021b-95d7-4e41-a7c3-9a17b520496a",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Requirement fidelity (rules/system/requirement-fidelity)"
      },
      {
        "id": "b2ec8b4f-87da-453f-802f-d2bcf092e56b",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Command discipline (rules/system/command-discipline)"
      }
    ],
    "examples": [],
    "kind": "skill",
    "onFailure": [
      {
        "id": "d4cda87b-45c4-40d0-9f35-1e55c2d23037",
        "text": "Read the CLI error — it names the fix; correct the call and retry once"
      },
      {
        "id": "04c4444d-6561-47eb-b7f5-f71ffe3bd21e",
        "text": "NEVER fall back to editing .pebble files directly, whatever failed"
      },
      {
        "id": "e827ce91-3bc3-4149-b7f6-d4b9834d39fa",
        "text": "If still blocked, report the exact command and error to the user and stop"
      }
    ],
    "output": "The fix in code, statuses updated truthfully, and a finding documenting what was broken and what changed.",
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "id": "add9819b-e829-44dc-a0a3-3f5792bd2c54",
        "text": "A saved map — locate the code via the graph, not grep"
      },
      {
        "id": "f48ed8e7-3b76-4482-93c4-660b94da61d9",
        "text": "The failing pebble/unit and the spec↔code gap are identified before editing"
      }
    ],
    "purpose": "Fix the code so it satisfies a spec (records the fix)",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "25bcd184-9d4e-400f-9376-c66c0b1a3cc3",
        "text": "Fix the implementation so it satisfies this spec: $ARGUMENTS"
      },
      {
        "id": "a3ad6bd9-d772-4f44-9df8-3a85510997e8",
        "text": "SCOPE FIRST (echo before editing): the pebble/unit that is failing, the exact gap between spec and code, and the files you will touch. Fixing the wrong gap is wasted work."
      },
      {
        "id": "06d59c11-a16d-4e4a-a5df-ddab4a72d41a",
        "text": "STEP 1 — GROUND IT: `get` the pebble + its refs (honor model/contract shapes exactly); locate the code via the graph (map-symbol/map-search/map-callers), read the FULL surrounding context, and cite a precedent file for any pattern you introduce."
      },
      {
        "id": "fcb8ccaf-11bf-4101-bbcd-c4afd18d5610",
        "text": "STEP 2 — FIX MINIMALLY: change only what the spec requires, following the codebase's own conventions. Do NOT redesign the spec — a spec that is itself wrong becomes an assumption/spec-violation finding for the user, never a silent code decision."
      },
      {
        "id": "24a09d2b-6123-478d-824d-1498367253c3",
        "text": "STEP 3 — PROVE IT: run the relevant gates (build/lint/tests) in the project's sanctioned runtime; judge by EXIT CODE, not log text; re-run after your LAST edit. A gate you did not run is a gate that did not pass."
      },
      {
        "id": "b7468212-bd47-4886-a998-2ee0f43761e0",
        "text": "STEP 4 — RECORD: set truthful statuses (implemented = code exists; leave verified to the verifier unless you proved behavior), then \"{PEBBLES_CLI}\" add-finding <path> --title \"...\" [--unit <id>] --category bug --observation \"what was broken\" --evidence \"file:line\" --solution \"what you changed\"."
      },
      {
        "id": "f8898672-fbdf-4166-b285-8e9b73d83346",
        "text": "Report: what you changed, which gates passed (with their exit results), and any spec gap you flagged rather than guessed."
      }
    ],
    "verify": [
      {
        "id": "33d86019-45e9-4a4a-893a-05629a1ba880",
        "text": "The relevant gates passed by EXIT CODE, re-run after the last edit"
      },
      {
        "id": "f312b410-7d70-4a49-8383-d3da739a5416",
        "text": "Only the spec's gap was changed; any wrong-spec was flagged as a finding, not silently redesigned"
      },
      {
        "id": "de8a392f-cf55-4dbc-89af-1aedfd8f289c",
        "text": "Statuses updated truthfully and a finding records what was broken and what changed"
      }
    ],
    "whenToUse": "Making the code satisfy a spec it currently fails — find via the graph, change, check, record."
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.785Z",
  "description": "Fix the code so it satisfies a spec (records the fix)",
